-------------------------- SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS -------------------------------

Any *NIX-alike (or POSIX compliant) system with a C compiler.

For a fairly complete list of all C-library references done in the programs
see "src/includes.h".

Builds clean (warning-free) with either the system "cc"/clang/gcc or with
the Zig toolchain's C compiler ("zig cc") as a drop-in CC replacement:

  make CC="zig cc"

See INSTALL for details.

------------------------------ DESCRIPTION -----------------------------------

lockfile creates one or more semaphore files, retrying and waiting until it
succeeds or a retry/timeout limit is reached. It's most commonly used to
serialize access to a mailbox before invoking a mail reader that doesn't
know how to lock mailboxes itself.

See the lockfile(1) man page (man/lockfile.man) for full usage.

